{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Abram</b> — twice at the beginning of a verse: here and the other is אברם הוא אברהם (Abram, he is Abraham). And this is what the Sages interpreted: every place where \"he is\" is stated, he was righteous from beginning to end. And this is \"he is Abram, he is Abraham\" — righteous from beginning to end. Therefore \"Abram dwelt\" to separate from Lot the wicked."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:16:02.003129059Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}